"""Extra original pedagogical guidance for every actual TaalCompleet KNM chapter.

The chapter titles, factual subjects and textbook pagination are stored in
course_content.json; this module adds English explanation and accessible
study activities, not excerpts or newly invented publisher chapters.
"""

DEEP = {
'1.1': ("Maps and administration", "The capital is Amsterdam; the national government operates from The Hague. Province boundaries, municipalities and travel routes are different kinds of geographic information. Think of a journey: find a place, decide which city is relevant, then check how to travel.", "Amsterdam is not the place where all Dutch government ministries sit.", "Amsterdam is de hoofdstad. De regering werkt in Den Haag."),
'1.2': ("Living with water", "Separate prevention from reclamation. Dikes and dunes help protect against high water; a polder is land where water levels are managed. The flood disaster of 1953 explains why long-term flood defences are important.", "A dike, a dune and a polder are not the same structure.", "Een dijk beschermt ons tegen hoog water."),
'1.3': ("Trade and its human cost", "Shipping and overseas trade contributed to economic wealth for Dutch trading interests in the seventeenth century. The wider history also includes colonial control, forced labour and slavery. Explain a historical fact without ignoring who may have been exploited.", "Overseas trade is not the same thing as freedom for everyone involved.", "Nederlandse schepen voeren naar veel landen."),
'1.4': ("Colonial history", "A colony is governed or controlled by an outside power. The Dutch colonial past involved Asian and Caribbean regions. Distinguish the power relationship from voluntary tourism or ordinary present-day international trade.", "Slavery cannot be described as an ordinary voluntary job.", "Vroeger had Nederland koloniën."),
'1.5': ("War, remembrance and freedom", "Nazi Germany occupied the Netherlands during World War II. The Holocaust involved the persecution and murder of Jewish people and other groups. On 4 May many people commemorate war victims; 5 May celebrates liberation and freedom.", "4 May is remembrance; 5 May is celebration.", "Op 4 mei herdenken we de slachtoffers."),
'1.6': ("Life after 1945", "The Netherlands rebuilt after the war. Economic change, migration and new social attitudes shaped a more diverse population. KNM connects this historical development to everyday citizenship and dealing respectfully with people of different backgrounds.", "Shared legal rights do not mean everyone must have identical customs.", "Nederland is na de oorlog veranderd."),
'1.7': ("History recall", "Practice by explaining the sequence map → water → trade → colonies → occupation → postwar change. Speak one complete A2 sentence for each stage. A short daily self-test is more useful than rereading the same paragraph without recall.", "Textbook review worksheets may need the publisher's separate online learning environment.", "Ik kan de zes onderwerpen in eigen woorden uitleggen."),
'2.1': ("A realistic home search", "A woonwens is the combination of things you hope for: location, size, neighbourhood, transport and affordability. Separate what you want from what your income and local housing supply make possible.", "A preferred home is not automatically an affordable or available home.", "Ik zoek een betaalbare woning dicht bij mijn werk."),
'2.2': ("Finding housing", "Social rental housing and private rental housing have different access and allocation arrangements. Follow legitimate channels, check eligibility and ask what documents are needed. Registration waiting times and financial thresholds can change.", "Registration with a housing association is not a guarantee of an immediate home.", "Ik schrijf me in en controleer de voorwaarden."),
'2.3': ("Before signing", "A rental contract sets out rent, payments, responsibilities and conditions. Consider deposit, utilities, service costs, maintenance and notice periods. Ask questions before signing and preserve a copy of the agreement.", "A deposit is not simply an extra monthly rent payment.", "Ik lees eerst het huurcontract."),
'2.4': ("Housing money categories", "A municipal tax, insurance policy and housing allowance solve different things. Waste-collection fees finance a service, home contents insurance can protect belongings, and rent allowance may help eligible tenants with housing costs.", "A tax paid to a municipality is not a voluntary insurance policy.", "Ik controleer mijn belasting, verzekering en toeslag."),
'2.5': ("Utilities and problems", "When moving, identify who supplies water, gas and electricity, take meter readings and check contract conditions. For a fault, identify whether the responsibility lies with a supplier, grid operator, landlord or maintenance contractor.", "A fixed energy price does not necessarily make the whole final bill fixed.", "Ik geef de meterstanden door."),
'2.6': ("Waste and neighbourhood", "Municipalities organise household-waste collection, and the local sorting rules may vary. Recycling is easier when you know what belongs in paper, glass, organic waste, packaging and residual waste categories.", "Do not assume collection schedules are identical in every town.", "Ik kijk op de afvalkalender van mijn gemeente."),
'2.7': ("Housing review", "Explain one full journey: deciding where to live, finding a property, reading a tenancy agreement, arranging utilities, understanding charges and putting rubbish in the right place. Turn each step into a practical situation.", "Review summaries are not a substitute for reading contract conditions.", "Eerst zoek ik een huis, daarna regel ik de kosten."),
'3.1': ("Choosing first medical contact", "The huisarts is generally the first point of contact for everyday medical problems. For urgent but non-life-threatening issues when the practice is closed, contact the huisartsenpost. In immediately life-threatening emergencies use 112.", "A routine GP appointment and a life-threatening emergency are not the same.", "Ik bel de huisarts voor een gewone medische klacht."),
'3.2': ("Referrals and specialist care", "A GP can arrange a referral to a medical specialist where medically appropriate. A referral is an administrative and clinical route, not a guarantee that every proposed treatment is covered or immediately available.", "Seeing a specialist often requires different steps from contacting your own GP.", "De huisarts geeft mij een verwijzing."),
'3.3': ("Collecting medicines", "Prescription medicines are obtained through a pharmacy. The textbook also mentions non-prescription products available at drugstores. Read doses and warnings, and ask a pharmacist if you are unsure; do not assume similar-looking medicines are interchangeable.", "A prescription is not necessary for every medicine, but many medicines do require one.", "Ik haal mijn medicijnen bij de apotheek."),
'3.4': ("Dentist and social appointments", "Choose a dental practice, register if accepted and arrange checks. The book describes making appointments, punctuality and cancelling in advance. A missed appointment may be charged depending on conditions and timing.", "An appointment culture is a social norm, while cancellation fees depend on conditions.", "Ik bel als ik tien minuten te laat kom."),
'3.5': ("From pregnancy to birth registration", "Distinguish the verloskundige (pregnancy/birth care), kraamzorg (support around and after birth) and consultatiebureau (infant development and prevention). The book also describes registering a baby's birth at the municipality and customs such as kraambezoek.", "Registering a birth is an official process; giving a geboortekaartje is a custom.", "We maken een afspraak voor het kraambezoek."),
'3.6': ("What is covered by insurance", "Adults generally must have qualifying Dutch basic health insurance. Extra supplementary insurance is optional. A premium is different from the annual mandatory deductible (eigen risico), and some services have an additional contribution (eigen bijdrage). Coverage rules can change.", "An ordinary GP consultation is exempt from the compulsory deductible.", "Ik vergelijk de basisverzekering en een aanvullende verzekering."),
'3.7': ("Donor register decisions", "The Donorregister records a person's organ and tissue donation choice for after death. The registration system has legal rules and choices; it is not the same as donating blood or getting a transplant appointment.", "Registration and discussing your wishes with family are different, complementary steps.", "Ik lees informatie over het Donorregister."),
'3.8': ("Healthcare review", "Practise choosing the correct organisation in three stories: a non-urgent cough, an urgent problem at night and a life-threatening accident. Then contrast specialist referrals, pharmacy prescriptions, insurance and care for newborn babies.", "Do not choose 112 merely because a problem feels inconvenient.", "Ik kijk eerst welke zorg ik nodig heb."),
'4.1': ("School structures", "Children can start primary school at four; school attendance normally becomes compulsory at five. The primary and secondary routes lead to different further education possibilities. School choice and special education support can require individual arrangements.", "Starting school at age four and compulsory attendance from five are different rules.", "Mijn kind gaat vanaf vijf jaar verplicht naar school."),
'4.2': ("Parents and teachers", "Parent participation can include school trips and celebrations. Ouder­gesprekken focus on development and behaviour. The book illustrates a teacher communicating directly and parents cooperating, but helping at every classroom activity is not a general obligation.", "The school's voluntary parent contribution is not a compulsory school-entry fee.", "Ik maak een afspraak met de juf."),
'4.3': ("Further education routes", "VMBO, HAVO and VWO are secondary routes. After secondary school, opportunities may include MBO, HBO and university study, subject to qualifications and admission requirements. Try connecting an occupation with the relevant education route.", "MBO, HBO and WO do not refer to the same education level.", "Na het vmbo kun je vaak een mbo-opleiding volgen."),
'4.4': ("Holidays and absences", "School holiday calendars vary by region and school, and some teacher-training days differ locally. Sinterklaas, Christmas, Easter, Eid and carnival may be celebrated differently. Check whether leave is automatically allowed or needs an application.", "A celebration does not always mean every school is closed.", "Ik kijk wanneer de schoolvakantie begint."),
'4.5': ("Parenting and safety", "Parenting includes caring, guidance and recognising children’s boundaries and development. Dutch schools and services can help families. Physical punishment and violence are not permitted; family custom is not a defence for abuse.", "A parent can set household rules without using violence.", "We praten rustig met ons kind."),
'4.6': ("Childcare and education bills", "Distinguish childcare fees and possible childcare allowance from ordinary school costs. Primary education is funded publicly, while parents buy supplies and may be asked for a voluntary contribution for extra activities.", "A voluntary school contribution must not be treated as a mandatory admission charge.", "Ik controleer of ik recht heb op kinderopvangtoeslag."),
'4.7': ("School review", "Tell the complete learner journey from primary school to secondary routes and later training. Practise attendance rules, parent-teacher communication, holiday arrangements and childcare support with examples.", "A single school may organise activities differently from another school.", "Ik weet wat ik aan de school kan vragen."),
'5.1': ("Skills and qualifications", "A talent is something you may do well; a skill is something you can often practise or demonstrate. Identify your strengths with evidence and consider whether foreign diplomas need to be assessed for a job or course.", "An experience certificate does not automatically equal a formal diploma.", "Ik ben goed in samenwerken en ik kan plannen."),
'5.2': ("Finding vacancies", "A vacancy describes tasks and required experience. Search through reliable platforms, employer pages or employment services. Compare job requirements with your skills and record the deadline and contact details.", "A vacancy is a job opportunity, not a contract.", "Ik zoek een vacature en lees de eisen."),
'5.3': ("Applying and interviews", "A CV describes education, work experience and skills. An application letter explains your interest. In an interview, prepare examples of your work and questions about tasks; send documents securely.", "A CV and a motivation letter have different purposes.", "Ik schrijf een brief en maak een cv."),
'5.4': ("Contracts and working conditions", "Employment agreements describe hours, pay, leave and duration. A cao may establish collective minimum conditions. Many employers discuss work performance in a review meeting; negotiation can be appropriate but rights and bargaining outcomes depend on circumstances.", "A fixed contract normally has no specified end date; a temporary contract does.", "Ik lees mijn contract voordat ik onderteken."),
'5.5': ("Payslips and annual statements", "Gross pay is the amount before applicable deductions; net pay is what you receive after them. A payslip shows period-level details, and an annual statement summarises wages and deductions across a tax year.", "Your contract's gross wage is not necessarily the sum sent to your bank.", "Op mijn loonstrook staan bruto en netto."),
'5.6': ("Rights beyond pay", "Work also involves rest periods, holidays, sickness reporting and workplace safety. Find out who to contact about unsafe conditions or problems with an employer and which agreements apply.", "A normal workplace disagreement is not automatically the same as a legal rights violation.", "Ik vraag hoe verlof en ziekte geregeld zijn."),
'5.7': ("Starting a business", "Running a business involves customers, costs and administration. Entrepreneurs typically need to consider Chamber of Commerce registration, taxes, invoices and insurance. Requirements vary by type of work.", "Being self-employed is not the same as having an employee's working contract.", "Ik controleer of ik mij bij de KVK moet inschrijven."),
'5.8': ("Benefits and the right desk", "WW is unemployment insurance administered by UWV. Bijstand is means-tested support normally handled by the municipality. Eligibility, duties and reporting rules depend on personal circumstances, so the location of help is as important as the name of the benefit.", "WW and bijstand are not two names for the same benefit.", "Voor WW kijk ik bij het UWV."),
'5.9': ("Employment review", "Follow the journey from personal talent to vacancy, application, contract, payslip and any later change in work. Finish by explaining where to ask for support when employment ends or working conditions are unsafe.", "A good exam answer depends on the situation, not only the word 'werk'.", "Ik kan uitleggen hoe je werk zoekt."),
'6.1': ("Municipal services", "The gemeente handles resident registration, many local permits, documents and certain support services. The correct municipality depends on where you live and what you need; appointments and identity requirements often apply.", "The municipality does not make national laws on its own.", "Ik geef mijn verhuizing door aan de gemeente."),
'6.2': ("Urgent and non-urgent help", "112 is for urgent emergencies involving danger to life, safety or serious situations needing immediate response. For police matters without urgency, the book gives 0900-8844. Healthcare also has GP and out-of-hours GP routes.", "The police, ambulance and fire brigade have different services, but 112 connects emergency help.", "Bij direct gevaar bel ik 112."),
'6.3': ("Taxes and online identity", "The Belastingdienst manages taxes. An invitation to file an income-tax return generally requires filing within applicable deadlines; not every resident files automatically every year. DigiD is a secure login method and must be protected.", "A BSN identifies you; it is not your login password.", "Ik lees de brief van de Belastingdienst goed."),
'6.4': ("Choosing the right help", "Financial problems may call for municipal debt services; food assistance may involve a food bank; legal advice may involve a legal help service. Explain your problem clearly, preserve letters and observe deadlines.", "A klacht about treatment is different from bezwaar against a formal decision.", "Ik vraag hulp bij schulden aan de gemeente."),
'6.5': ("Institutions review", "Given an unfamiliar problem, ask first: Is it urgent? Is it local registration, taxation, employment insurance, debt or a legal dispute? That decision tree usually leads to the right organisation.", "Official online services should be accessed through trusted domains, not suspicious messages.", "Ik kies de instantie die bij mijn probleem past."),
'7.1': ("Democracy and voting", "Actief kiesrecht means the right to vote; passief kiesrecht means the right to stand for election. Eligibility differs for national, municipal and other elections. The Netherlands is a representative democracy.", "Living in the Netherlands alone does not make everyone eligible to vote in the Tweede Kamer election.", "Ik controleer of ik bij een verkiezing mag stemmen."),
'7.2': ("Three administrative layers", "National government, provinces and municipalities have different tasks. The Tweede Kamer has 150 members and the Eerste Kamer 75. The constitutional regering consists of the King and ministers; the kabinet includes ministers and state secretaries.", "The Eerste Kamer and Tweede Kamer have different roles and membership numbers.", "De Tweede Kamer heeft honderdvijftig leden."),
'7.3': ("Separation of powers", "The legislature makes law, the executive implements it and the judiciary decides legal disputes and criminal cases. Courts must be independent. Appeals depend on the kind of proceeding and its procedural rules.", "A minister cannot dictate an independent court's judgment.", "De rechter beslist onafhankelijk."),
'7.4': ("Rights and legal boundaries", "Article 1 concerns equal treatment. Other protections cover religion, expression, privacy and personal autonomy. Threats, coercion and violence are not excused by invoking freedom; sensitive medical decisions operate within strict legal conditions.", "Not all different treatment is discrimination; the legal context matters.", "Iedereen heeft recht op gelijke behandeling."),
'7.5': ("Final source-book review", "The book teaches a computer-based interface and advises checking unanswered questions. It prints older claims of 40 questions and 70% passing. Current DUO information confirms a 45-minute computer exam and content updates from July 2025; use the current official practice questions.", "This app's 20-question quizzes and 16/20 goal are not the official exam scoring system.", "Ik lees rustig en controleer mijn antwoorden."),
}

assert len(DEEP)==48, f'Expected 48 chapters, got {len(DEEP)}'

# Practical, thematic concept lenses used to link a single book section with its wider theme.
CONCEPT_LENS = {
1: [('Map / geography', 'Choose a province, capital, government seat or travel route.'), ('Water management', 'Decide whether the question concerns a dike, polder or flood history.'), ('History and remembrance', 'Place an event in the seventeenth century, colonial period, World War II or postwar years.')],
2: [('Find', 'Decide what type of housing fits your needs and what registration is required.'), ('Agree', 'Read rent, deposit, maintenance and notice conditions.'), ('Live', 'Arrange utilities, understand taxes and sort waste correctly.')],
3: [('Triage', 'Routine GP → urgent out-of-hours GP → immediate danger 112.'), ('Treatment', 'Understand referral, specialist care and pharmacy roles.'), ('Payment and family', 'Distinguish basic/supplementary insurance, deductible, birth care and organ donation.')],
4: [('Attendance', 'Know when children start school and when school is compulsory.'), ('Communication', 'Parent-teacher meetings and school activities.'), ('Routes and costs', 'VMBO/HAVO/VWO, MBO/HBO/WO, childcare and holiday rules.')],
5: [('Get a job', 'Talent → vacancy → application → interview.'), ('At work', 'Contract → cao → gross/net payslip → workplace rights.'), ('Change', 'Business, unemployment and appropriate benefit administration.')],
6: [('Local life', 'Municipal registration and support.'), ('Safety', '112 for immediate danger, otherwise appropriate non-emergency channels.'), ('Administration', 'Tax returns, DigiD, debt help, complaints and objections.')],
7: [('Choose', 'Democracy and eligibility to vote.'), ('Govern', 'Parliament, government, cabinet and local levels.'), ('Protect', 'Courts, fundamental rights and legal limits on power.')],
}

